## 13. API Data Flow

The required data flow:

```
Database
   |
   v
SQLAlchemy Model
   |
   v
Service
   |
   v
Pydantic VO
   |
   v
ApiResponse[T]
   |
   v
FastAPI JSON Response
```

Never:

```
Database
   |
   v
dict
   |
   v
Router
   |
   v
JSON
```

---

## 14. Refactoring Rules

When modifying existing code:

1. Do not refactor the whole project at once.
2. Modify one module at a time.
3. Preserve existing JSON structure.
4. Add response_model before changing implementation.
5. Run type checking after every module.

Recommended order:

```
1. app/utils/response.py

2. app/schemas/vo

3. app/services

4. app/routers
```

---

## 15. Code Review Checklist

Before commit, check:

Forbidden:
```
return dict
return JSONResponse
return ORM Model from Router
model_dump() in Router
VO.model_dump() for API output
__dict__
dict(model)
ApiResponse[Any]
```

Required:
```
Every endpoint:
    response_model=ApiResponse[T]

Every Router (except login):
    current_user via Depends(get_current_user)  # 仅 me/touch/logout
    OR Depends(require_perm(Perm.XXX)) / require_any_perm / require_admin_user  # 业务路由

Every business Router:
    no bare get_current_user without Perm
    no permission string literals — use Perm.*

Every write Router → Service:
    pass current_user=current_user

Every Router:
    returns ApiResponse[T]

Every Service:
    returns VO
    no implicit current_user / ContextVar

Every Repository:
    returns SQLAlchemy Model

Frontend (same codes):
    menu → canAccessPage / applySidebarPermissions
    button → can('op:…')
    details → docs/permission-design.md
```
